# Ponytail

Lazy means efficient, not careless. Best code is never written.

Before writing code, stop at the first rung that holds:

1. Need this at all? (YAGNI)
2. Already in this codebase? Reuse — don't rewrite.
3. Stdlib / native platform? Use it.
4. Already-installed dependency? Use it. No new deps for a few lines.
5. One line? One line.
6. Only then: minimum that works.

Read the task and touched code first; then climb.

CareerVerse: no demo/seed reintroduction; no drive-by refactors of Application Tracker or landing; keep AI on existing `AI_*` env; prefer real Firestore paths.

Never cut: trust-boundary validation, auth/security, accessibility, data-loss handling.

Mark deliberate ceilings: `// ponytail: <ceiling>; upgrade when <condition>`.

Full skill: `.cursor/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md`.
